ios: host menus, pinch zoom, HUD stats (mobile HUD v2)

For the redesigned mobile HUD (ios/web/host):

- Host menus: with setHostMenus(true) the host shows the options menu itself, as a large menu for fingers, instead of
  the drawn 15 px rows. The client then neither draws the open menu nor picks from it or closes it on its own (the
  long-press release, the pointer moving away, a click that reaches it anyway only closes it); the host picks an option
  with hudMenuSelect(serial, index) or closes it with hudMenuClose(serial), handled at the start of the next mouseLoop
  like a click on the menu; a close that follows a pick of the same menu before that cycle does not undo the pick. Every
  menu opened gets a new serial, so a pick for a menu that has meanwhile closed does nothing, and 'menu-open' (now with
  the serial) is reported again when a menu closes and another opens within one cycle. 'menu-open' also names the finger
  that opened the menu with a long-press (pointerId, while it is still down; -1 for a tap in right-click mode or a
  mouse), so the host can follow that finger for press-drag-release instead of guessing it. hudMenu() returns the open
  menu.
- Pinch zoom: setCameraZoom(zoom) scales the orbit camera's distance (pitch * 3 + 600) by 0.6..1.4 (any closer and the
  camera ends up inside the walls of small rooms). The tile
  visibility matrix (World.resetVisCalc) is relative to the camera, and a zoom only changes the camera's height by a
  factor, so one matrix with the frustum's height range widened by hMax * (1 - 0.6) below and hMax * (1.4 - 1) above
  (hMax = the camera height at the steepest pitch, about 1690) covers every zoom. It is computed once, at maininit and
  when the viewport changes size, instead of again for each new zoom: a recompute takes 60-85 ms (desktop) to 260 ms
  (4x CPU throttle), which stalled the frames while pinching. Tiles at the edge of a zoomed-out view are not culled.
- Touch tuning: TOUCH_SLOP 14 px (was 10): a finger resting on a target for a long-press may wander that far, and an
  item drag or list scroll starts only past it. The default long-press is 400 ms (was 450).
- On a touch screen the top-left tooltip ("Walk here / 2 more options") is drawn only while a finger is down: the
  pointer only hovers then, and the text was left behind after every tap. A use or target mode that a tap selected
  keeps its prompt there ("Use Tinderbox with...", "Cast Wind Strike on...", not the option last under the finger),
  as nothing else on screen shows that mode.
- hudState() adds hp/hpMax and prayer/prayerMax (the HUD's orbs), cameraYaw (its compass) and cameraZoom;
  hudFaceNorth() turns the camera north (the compass button).

